From: jonathansong <7958352+jonathansong@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] [TensorExt] Keep the insert's destination when folding insert_slice into dispatch.tensor.store

FoldInsertSliceWithTensorStoreOp rewrote store(insert_slice(src into dest))
as a store of src at the slice only, dropping dest: correct only when dest
is undefined (tensor.empty). A chain of insert_slices (a dispatch putting
its rows together into one result) kept only its last row, the earlier
rows' computations then dead code. dest is now stored first unless it is a
tensor.empty, so a chain folds into one store per slice. Found by the sa
plugin's prefill attention chunks (docs/fusion_design.md §6.7).

diff --git a/compiler/src/iree/compiler/Dialect/TensorExt/Transforms/Folders.cpp b/compiler/src/iree/compiler/Dialect/TensorExt/Transforms/Folders.cpp
index 591fc68..8525e71 100644
--- a/compiler/src/iree/compiler/Dialect/TensorExt/Transforms/Folders.cpp
+++ b/compiler/src/iree/compiler/Dialect/TensorExt/Transforms/Folders.cpp
@@ -71,6 +71,17 @@ struct FoldInsertSliceWithTensorStoreOp
       return failure();
     }
 
+    // The rest of the stored value is the insert's destination: unless it is
+    // undefined (tensor.empty), it is stored first, as the original store did.
+    if (!insertSliceOp.getDest().getDefiningOp<tensor::EmptyOp>()) {
+      IREE::TensorExt::DispatchTensorStoreOp::create(
+          rewriter, dispatchTensorStoreOp.getLoc(), insertSliceOp.getDest(),
+          dispatchTensorStoreOp.getTarget(),
+          dispatchTensorStoreOp.getTargetDims(),
+          dispatchTensorStoreOp.getMixedOffsets(),
+          dispatchTensorStoreOp.getMixedSizes(),
+          dispatchTensorStoreOp.getMixedStrides());
+    }
     rewriter.replaceOpWithNewOp<IREE::TensorExt::DispatchTensorStoreOp>(
         dispatchTensorStoreOp, insertSliceOp.getSource(),
         dispatchTensorStoreOp.getTarget(),
